From 2be8d926f66395b23ed27499b96a2314fd8c821f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:46:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] rpmsg: qcom_glink_rpm: Resume the FIFOs where the RPM
 left them

glink_rpm_probe() zeroes the TX head and the RX tail in message RAM.
That matches the RPM on a cold boot, but not in a kernel started by
kexec: the RPM's TX tail and RX head are wherever the previous kernel
left them. A zeroed TX head makes the RPM consume a wrap's worth of
stale FIFO contents as commands; on SM6375 (moto g82 5G) the RPM falls
over and takes the SoC with it about 0.13 s into the new kernel, with
the new kernel meanwhile reading the RPM's old replies from a zeroed RX
tail ("unhandled rx cmd: 20").

Set the TX head to the RPM's TX tail and the RX tail to the RPM's RX
head instead: nothing pending in either direction, whatever state the
FIFOs are in. On a cold boot these are zero, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_rpm.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_rpm.c b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_rpm.c
index e3ba2c63a..1c05500f2 100644
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_rpm.c
@@ -339,8 +339,14 @@ static int glink_rpm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	rpm->tx_pipe.native.write = glink_rpm_tx_write;
 	rpm->tx_pipe.native.kick = glink_rpm_tx_kick;
 
-	writel(0, rpm->tx_pipe.head);
-	writel(0, rpm->rx_pipe.tail);
+	/*
+	 * Start where the RPM is, not at zero. After a kexec the FIFOs are in
+	 * use: rewinding our TX head makes the RPM take stale FIFO contents
+	 * for commands (and fall over), rewinding our RX tail replays the
+	 * RPM's old replies to us. On a cold boot both are at zero anyway.
+	 */
+	writel(readl(rpm->tx_pipe.tail), rpm->tx_pipe.head);
+	writel(readl(rpm->rx_pipe.head), rpm->rx_pipe.tail);
 
 	glink = qcom_glink_native_probe(dev,
 					0,
